.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
Unless \fB\-\-no\-config\fR is passed, scrcpy loads options from a configuration file before processing command-line options.

The default path is \fI%APPDATA%\\scrcpy\\config.ini\fR on Windows and \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/scrcpy/config.ini\fR on other platforms, falling back to \fI$HOME/.config/scrcpy/config.ini\fR when \fIXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is unset. Portable builds use \fIconfig.ini\fR next to the scrcpy executable.

Each non-empty line contains one long option without the leading "--". An option value is separated by "=". Leading and trailing spaces are ignored. A "#" starts a comment when it is the first non-space character or is preceded by whitespace, except when it is the first character of an option value.

Options before the first section apply globally.
A section defines a named profile, selected by passing its name as the
positional \fIprofile\fR argument.
Profile names are case-sensitive.
Without a profile argument, only global options are loaded.

For example:

.nf
    # Global defaults
    video-bit-rate = 8M

    [phone]
    serial = 192.168.1.10:5555
    max-size = 1080

    [tablet]
    serial = 192.168.1.20:5555
    max-size = 1600
.fi

For example, \fBscrcpy phone\fR loads the global options and the
\fB[phone]\fR section.
Command-line options are processed last.

Use \fB\-\-config\-file\fR or \fISCRCPY_CONFIG_FILE\fR to select another file.


